n: 3.13.1.8
name: why-rewrite-did-not-carry
kind: finding
is: The C rewrite replaced the C and kept the contract: the 124-name primitive registry, two surface grammars and the band pins. Its hours went into covering the old surface again in new C, and its one new part, a frame interpreter over values passed as wide structs, was slower than the old seed's walker, in which integers ride as tagged words.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.1.2 3.13.1.3 3.13.1.4 3.13.1.5
conf: mid
limit: The speed gap is recorded once and its cause was not profiled.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2
name: carrier
kind: hub
is: The greenfield carrier is one commit of 2026-11-05 that nothing later touches: a 64-bit word of 0, 1, nothing or node, immutable cells, offer as the only act, machine-code leaves and eleven doors, with no reader or evaluator. Its 31 checks pass on one arm64 Mac. Its production proof bypasses the membrane, its store never reuses a slot, a shared child doubles canonical bytes, and its x86-64 leaf returns the wrong number.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.3
name: word-and-held
kind: observation
is: The carrier's 64-bit word is 0 for state 0, 1 for state 1, 2 for nothing and (slot << 2) | 3 for a node. Held work is not a word: offer returns arrived = 0 and no ack. That outcome has one producer, event.wait with a non-zero argument on an empty pipe. The Held table is never read, and a leaf calling back gets nothing for an offer not arrived.
status: observed
src: 2.1.9#10-16 2.1.8#94-110 2.1.8#124-129 2.1.8#813 2.1.8#598
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.4
name: store-and-identity
kind: observation
is: A carrier cell is immutable, with at most 32 inline children and a 1 MiB payload, in a fixed table of 8,192 slots. Its canonical bytes hold each child's whole canonical bytes, not a digest. An FNV-1a 64 digest is computed and stored but finds nothing: compose deduplicates by comparing bytes with every live cell in turn, and a slot is never reused.
status: observed
src: 2.1.8#22-27 2.1.8#223-259 2.1.9#18-21
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.5
name: offer-dispatch
kind: observation
is: The carrier's offer returns {arrived, ack} and dispatches on the target's kind. A data cell acks itself; a port runs a C door; a leaf or export enters machine code; a channel with no arguments maps every leaf executable, enters none and acks 1; a channel with arguments mints a new channel and leaves the old one unchanged. A breach acks state 0.
status: observed
src: 2.1.9#103-106 2.1.8#543-556 2.1.8#914-989 2.1.8#135-140
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.6
name: ports-three-answers
kind: observation
is: A carrier port is a cell (direction, shape, name) with the six shapes and two directions of the host-kernel spec; eleven names are registered at open. An unknown name acks nothing; a known name with another direction or shape acks state 0 and leaves a breach row. Each carrier counts offers and nothings. A registered but absent carrier also acks 0.
status: observed
src: 2.1.8#476-495 2.1.8#874-912 2.1.8#447 2.1.9#39-44 2.21.4#86-91
limit: The absent-carrier path was read, not run: the one Mac used has both entropy and Metal. The header promises nothing for a missing driver.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.7
name: leaf-abi
kind: observation
is: A carrier leaf is a cell whose payload is one ABI byte and raw machine code of at most one page, mapped by one MAP_JIT mmap per leaf. Under ABI 1 the leaf is called as f(words, argc, offer): the callback arrives as an argument, so leaf code holds no absolute address. A scalar argument holding 0 or 1 reaches an ABI-1 leaf as the state word 0 or 1.
status: observed
src: 2.1.8#558-584 2.1.8#634-653 2.1.9#32-35
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.8
name: freeze-thaw-one-image
kind: observation
is: The carrier's freeze writes the magic FBOOT3 and the channel's canonical bytes twice, as declared identity and as graph. Thaw accepts only that format, rebuilds the graph in a fresh machine and leaves the caller unchanged on any mismatch. The only such image anything in the tree produces is the witness's four-cell example of 176 bytes.
status: observed
src: 2.1.8#1068-1090 2.1.8#1105-1124 2.21.2#138-144
limit: The two copies in one file detect damage to one of them; no digest is pinned outside the file.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.9
name: witness-run-31-checks
kind: finding
is: On 2026-11-24 the reading compiled the carrier and its witness from an unmodified membrane-boot.c with cc -O2 -Wall -Wextra in 0.19 s without diagnostics (binary 71,400 bytes) and ran it: 31 checks all 1, exit 0, page 16,384, arch aarch64, depth limit 1,022. One check enters a machine-code leaf with 40 and 2 and reads 42.
status: assumed
limit: One Apple arm64 machine. The witness copy differed from the repository file in seven path literals. The --produce half was not run.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.10
name: witness-gaps
kind: observation
is: The carrier's passing witness leaves two things unproved. Its x86-64 add leaf, bytes 01 fe 89 f8 c3, returns its first argument, 40 where the check expects 42, and its branch check fails by construction off aarch64. On aarch64 the branch check passes the same port for both arms and discards the 'no' path, so either arm writes the 'yes' file.
status: observed
src: 2.21.2#110 2.21.2#285-297
limit: Found by disassembly and reading; the witness was not run on x86-64.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.2.11
name: measured-limits
kind: observation
is: A probe linked against the unmodified carrier measured three limits. After about 4,000 top-level offers of clock.monotonic the store is full (8,191 live cells, 4,096 frame rows) and no released slot is reused. A node naming one child twice doubles its canonical bytes: 2,621,420 at level 16, refused at level 17. A file of 1,048,577 bytes reads as nothing.
status: observed
src: 2.1.8#256 2.1.8#22-27
limit: One machine. The offer count read 3,947 in the reading's run and 4,029, 4,034 and 4,019 in three reruns; the other figures reproduced exactly.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.3
name: standalone-bootstrap
kind: hub
is: What the two specs beside the axioms and the three ground files ask of a bootstrap, and what a new C bootstrap could take from the carrier: about 460 lines nearly unchanged and 530 to rewrite behind the same contract. The reading estimates 1,350 to 1,500 lines of C without a walker and 1,800 to 2,200 with one, under conditions the earlier attempts did not set. Nothing in the specs or the carrier says how the first image comes to exist.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.3.3
name: inherit-460-rewrite-530
kind: finding
is: Of membrane-boot.c's 1,199 lines about 460 can be inherited nearly unchanged: word and outcome constructors, host discovery, makers, executable mapping, the ABI-1 leaf entry, nine doors, byte codecs and the fault handler. About 530 keep their contract and need a new body: limits, compose, release, dispatch, frame rows, freeze and thaw.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.2.3 3.13.2.4 3.13.2.5 3.13.2.6 3.13.2.7 3.13.2.8 3.13.2.9 3.13.2.11
conf: mid
limit: Counted by reading on one machine and one architecture; 'nearly unchanged' means correct as read and exercised by a passing check.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.3.4
name: standalone-estimate
kind: finding
is: To stand alone the carrier lacks an entry, a store that scales, an image format for shared graphs, a walker or a binary seed, most doors and a code arena. The reading estimates a standalone C bootstrap at 1,350 to 1,500 lines with a binary seed per target, or 1,800 to 2,200 with a walker and a numeric seed, above the first round's 1,400 to 1,600.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.3.3 3.13.2.11 3.13.2.8 3.13.1.2
conf: low
limit: Scaled from measured sizes, not built; the rewrite overran its first size 6.5 times in 56 hours. Holds only if the walker runs one program, the compiler, written against about 25 primitives, and a line count gates from the first commit. The 100 to 150 lines for a strong digest in C are assumed.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Seven things to carry forward. From the carrier: the word that keeps nothing apart from state 0; equality by canonical bytes, with children named by identity; one offer entry with publication apart from entry and a callback passed to leaf code; ports with three distinct answers; minting, whole-image refusal and unresumed faults. From the rewrite and the notes: a second witness built first, and a build key of seed digest plus target.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.8.2
name: keep-equality-is-bytes-children-by-identity
kind: finding
is: Keep the rule that equality is the canonical bytes and a digest only indexes, and change the canonical form so that a cell names its children by identity instead of holding their bytes. In the carrier a shared child doubles the bytes at every level, and 16 levels reach 2,621,420 bytes.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.2.4 3.13.2.11 1.3
conf: high
limit: Whether a collision-resistant digest must exist in C or FNV may stay as an index is not settled.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.8.4
name: keep-port-three-answers
kind: finding
is: Keep ports as (direction, shape, name) with three distinct answers: an unknown name acks nothing; a wrong shape acks state 0 from the membrane and leaves a row; a present door gives its own ack. Keep a count of offers and of nothings per carrier.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.2.6 1.4 1.7.19
conf: high
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Seven things to let go: the old bands and registry as the acceptance test of a new floor; a second reader of the surface in C; wide struct values and a journal replayed by every process; doors chosen by a number that can differ between runtimes; fixed tables, path buffers and observations kept in the store they observe; titles and green checks that claim more than the code does; and landing a whole stack as one commit.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.13.9.1
name: drop-old-bands-as-acceptance-test
kind: finding
is: Do not judge a new floor by the old body's bands and primitive registry. The C rewrite was judged by whether it ran the existing body, and its seed went from 1,574 lines and 24 operations to 10,302 and 254 in 56 hours.
status: inferred
from: 3.13.1.2 3.13.1.3 3.13.1.8
conf: high
at: 2026-11-24

